==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Havsnejonöga.jpg|thumb|A '''lamprey''']]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|laumprei}}, adopted from {{bor|en|fro|lampreie}} (Modern {{m|fr|lamproie}}), from {{bor|en|ML.|lampreda}}, possibly alteration of {{der|en|LL.|lampetra|t=lamprey}}, whose further origin is unknown, though is [[folk etymology|traditionally]] thought to be a combination of {{compound|la|lambō|petra|gloss1=I lick, lap|gloss2=stone, rock}}. {{doublet|en|limpet}}, which came straightway from {{der|en|la|-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlæm.pɹi/|/ˈlæm.pɹeɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-ca-lamprey.opus|Audio (CA)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|lam|prey|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any long slender [[primitive]] eel-like [[freshwater]] and saltwater [[fish]] of the [[Petromyzontidae]] [[family]], having a [[sucking]] [[mouth]] with [[rasping]] [[teeth]] but no [[jaw]].

